# Grainlify backend configuration.
#
# Every variable internal/config/config.go reads is listed here, grouped by
# subsystem. Empty means "no default": the feature it belongs to is disabled
# or the process refuses to start, as noted per group.
#
# Keep this file in step with config.go. It previously listed 25 of 45
# variables, carried GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET twice, and documented APP_ROLE,
# which nothing reads.

# ─── Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DB_URL=
# Runs migrations on boot. Production has this on.
AUTO_MIGRATE=true
JWT_SECRET='dev-secret-change-me'
PORT=8080
# dev | production. Affects logging and a few guard rails.
APP_ENV=dev
LOG_LEVEL=info
# Comma-separated allowed origins for CORS. Empty allows the built-in defaults.
CORS_ORIGINS=
# One-time token for creating the first admin. Leave empty once one exists.
ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=
# Base64 32-byte key encrypting stored GitHub tokens. Rotating it invalidates
# every stored token.
TOKEN_ENC_KEY_B64=

# ─── URLs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the API is reachable from the internet. Used to build the GitHub App
# install callback and the Didit webhook callback, so a wrong value here means
# those callbacks point somewhere that does not answer.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# Where the frontend is. Used in notification emails.
FRONTEND_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ─── GitHub OAuth (sign-in) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must match the callback registered on the OAuth app exactly.
GITHUB_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:8080/auth/github/login/callback
GITHUB_OAUTH_SUCCESS_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:5173
# Legacy names, still read as a fallback if the OAUTH_ pair is unset.
GITHUB_LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL=
GITHUB_LOGIN_SUCCESS_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ─── GitHub App (repo access, webhooks) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Numeric, e.g. 123456
GITHUB_APP_ID=
# The name in the app's URL, e.g. github.com/apps/<slug>
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=
# PEM, base64-encoded. Raw PEM is also accepted; base64 avoids newline
# mangling in environment variables.
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ─── Identity verification (Didit) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# All three required for KYC. Missing any of them makes /kyc/start respond 503
# rather than failing silently.
DIDIT_API_KEY=
DIDIT_WORKFLOW_ID=
DIDIT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ─── Email (Mailercloud) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave MAILERCLOUD_API_KEY empty to disable email. In-app notifications work
# either way. EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS must be a verified sender in the account.
MAILERCLOUD_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=
EMAIL_FROM_NAME=Grainlify

# ─── Support widget sinks ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A support request is written to the database FIRST and delivered afterwards,
# so an unconfigured or failing sink never costs somebody their report and
# never changes their 200. An unset sink is skipped quietly - Telegram not
# being set up is not a Discord outage.
#
# Discord receives every category EXCEPT kyc. See the support-requests
# reference page for why that is enforced in code rather than by keeping the
# channel private.
DISCORD_BUG_REPORT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Telegram needs the token and chat id at minimum; a missing topic id degrades
# that category to the group's General thread rather than disabling the sink.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Numeric supergroup id, e.g. -1001234567890 - not an @handle.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# Numeric user id of the admin who receives KYC requests by direct message.
# KYC is never posted to the group, so if this is unset those requests reach
# nobody and the failure is logged at error level.
TELEGRAM_ADMIN_USER_ID=
# Forum topic ids within TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID, one per category.
TELEGRAM_TOPIC_BUGS=
TELEGRAM_TOPIC_KYC=
TELEGRAM_TOPIC_IDEAS=
TELEGRAM_TOPIC_HELP=
TELEGRAM_TOPIC_OTHER=

# ─── AI (hackathon judging) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ─── Message bus ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Empty falls back to the in-process bus.
NATS_URL=

# ─── Chain ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately empty. Nothing on the platform disburses funds on any chain and
# no contract has been deployed.
#
# Seven keys used to live here - four SOROBAN_* including a signing secret, plus
# three contract ids - read into config and consumed by nothing. They are gone.
# A signing-key variable that no code reads makes an unused key look
# provisioned and invites someone to wire something to it.
#
# When a real adapter lands, its configuration arrives with the code that reads
# it, and the key lives in a signer service rather than in this process.
#
# See the payout-path reference page for what is and is not built.
